  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nNo tricks with tonight's forecast! High pressure builds back \ninto the area with some shortwave energy bringing just enough \npassing cloud cover to increase the Halloween vibes. Ghosts and \nghouls will want a jacket tonight as temperatures start the \nevening in the low to mid 40s north, and in the upper 40s to low\n50s south, but they will be quickly dropping into the 30s by \nthe time the candy bowls run dry. Strong radiational cooling \ncontinues through the night with the first morning of November \nstarting out in the upper teens to mid-20s.\n\nTemperatures rebound quickly on Sunday as high pressure slides \nby to our south and starting up a warmer southwesterly flow. \nClear skies should allow temperatures to mix into the low to mid\n50s in the north, and into the upper 50s to near 60F in the \nsouth. This flow will raise dewpoints as well making for a \ncomparatively mild night in the upper 30s for most Sunday night.\nHigh pressure slowly continues eastward on Monday continuing \nwarm and dry conditions for much of the area, but low pressure \npassing to our north along with shortwave troughing aloft may \nbring some upslope showers to the higher terrain. Otherwise, \ndaytime temperatures climb into the low to mid 60s for the \nfoothills, with upper 60s to near 70F in the south. Temperatures\nare slightly cooler Tuesday as a weak backdoor cold front sinks\nsouthward. This front then lifts back north as a warm front and\nmay result in a few showers Tuesday night into Wednesday \nmorning as it does. Above normal temperatures look to continue \nthrough the remainder of the upcoming work week as ridging aloft\nremains firm.\n\nThe forecast going into late week remains very low confidence \nas global models have yet to come to any kind of consensus as to\nwhat might occur as troughing approaches the Eastern Seaboard. \nEnsembles have a fair signal for rain in this time frame, but \nthere has been no clear trend as fronts and systems continue to \nbounce around. The NBM was ready to go ahead and throw out \nlikely PoPs already, but I am not so confident and made sure \nthose were pulled back. It is certainly the window to watch \nright now, but that is all that can be said at this point.",
